From ec6d6af9e7dd3e04715426741d968df1dc0da269 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt C <latentcollapse@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 06:49:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 30/42] np2: name lost NeuraJL bindings, and reorient the model
 after compaction

- When the kernel dies, the error and the next call's notice list the lost
  bindings (name, type, call that set it) from the kernel's last reply.
- Base-tool factories may report their persistent state after compaction;
  NeuraJL lists its live bindings, as the IPython kernel's names already
  were.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../coding-agent/src/core/agent-session.ts    | 15 ++++++++++-
 .../coding-agent/src/core/tools/neurajl.ts    | 26 ++++++++++++++++---
 .../suite/neurajl-substrate-modes.test.ts     | 26 ++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 62 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

